# 21 — #2830 (owned FFI-buffer FIELD leak, Wave 2 Lane G): the new
# `isOwnedFfiBufferField` predicate (LlvmBackend_impl.hpp:6693) introduces
# one read at :6714, `dynamic_cast<const ast::FieldDecl*>(fs->decl)`.
# Structurally safe: the cast is preceded by `if (!fs->decl) { rt =
# ctx_.importedMemberType(fs); ... return ...; }` at :6711, so the cast
# only runs over LOCAL field symbols — the same guard pattern as the 20
# grandfathered reads in `isOwnedBuiltinExceptionField` (line 6656) /
# `isOwnedIteratorInterfaceField` (line 6749) / `isCapturedOwnedPrimary
# Param` (line 8548). The predicate is also wrapped in
# `isFfiBufferTypeRef(ctx_.importedMemberType(...))` which returns
# `nullptr` for the import path's {CString, WString, RawBytes} names —
# same shape as #2823's `registerUnwindOwnedParam` ffiBuffer arm.
# Re-baselined with `--force`; commit message of f3c20aa carries the
# load-bearing reasoning.
